WEBVTT

00:00:00.358 --> 00:00:02.371
Save fabric on every marker.

00:00:02.421 --> 00:00:07.978
BETA Cutting Room is free and open
source. It runs in your own factory.

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:12.731
A garment is cut from flat
shapes, called pattern pieces.

00:00:12.781 --> 00:00:17.711
A marker is the cutting plan: all
the pieces, laid on the fabric width.

00:00:17.761 --> 00:00:22.238
Pieces closer together make a
shorter marker, and use less fabric.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:28.523
Example: 10 cm shorter, on 50
layers, saves 5 metres of fabric.

00:00:28.573 --> 00:00:35.124
At ₹150 a metre, that is ₹750 saved on one lay.

00:00:35.174 --> 00:00:39.512
CAD software makes this
layout for you, and checks it.

00:00:40.142 --> 00:00:46.425
Many units still mark by hand, with
chalk. And commercial CAD is expensive.

00:00:47.051 --> 00:00:50.108
This is BETA Marker, with a demo shirt.

00:00:50.158 --> 00:00:54.887
Set the fabric width: 1500 mm.

00:00:54.937 --> 00:00:58.641
Set the size ratio: garments of each size.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.378
Press Nest. BETA places every piece for you.

00:01:03.428 --> 00:01:07.473
It tries many layouts,
and shows the best so far.

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:14.560
The result: marker length, and efficiency.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:19.410
Every marker is checked: no
overlaps, and the grain is right.

00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:23.159
Then export a PDF, or a plotter file.

00:01:25.751 --> 00:01:28.310
Cut plan turns an order into lays.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:31.970
Enter garments per size, and the highest ply.

00:01:33.605 --> 00:01:38.630
BETA works out the lays, the
plies, and the metres of fabric.

00:01:42.426 --> 00:01:45.400
Record each fabric roll and check it.

00:01:48.289 --> 00:01:50.841
Print a spreading sheet for each lay.

00:01:52.431 --> 00:01:56.464
Make bundles, with a QR ticket for every bundle.

00:01:59.529 --> 00:02:03.583
No CAD files? Use Quick Marker on your phone.

00:02:03.633 --> 00:02:07.862
Photograph the paper pieces,
with an A4 sheet for size.

00:02:07.912 --> 00:02:12.473
BETA finds the outlines. You
check and name each piece.

00:02:14.807 --> 00:02:17.919
Enter the fabric width and
the number of garments.

00:02:17.969 --> 00:02:20.081
Then BETA makes the marker.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:35.440
Print it on A4 sheets, use a
chalk guide, or a projector.

00:02:37.539 --> 00:02:41.229
BETA Pattern grades a pattern into all sizes.

00:02:42.811 --> 00:02:47.087
Seam checks show if two seams
that join have the same length.

00:02:51.344 --> 00:02:56.730
Export DXF files for your CAD,
or print the pieces full size.

00:02:57.357 --> 00:03:00.138
Is it good? We test it in public.

00:03:00.188 --> 00:03:12.090
300 Lectra tasks, 60 s each: BETA was 0.73 points
below Lectra on average, 1.22 below at the median.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:19.311
84 wins, 12 ties, 204 losses.
Close, but not better yet.

00:03:19.361 --> 00:03:22.539
And every marker is checked before export.

00:03:23.179 --> 00:03:27.127
Found a problem? Press Feedback, and tell us.

00:03:28.326 --> 00:03:33.474
BETA is free, works offline, and
your data stays in your factory.

00:03:33.524 --> 00:03:39.269
It is a young project, made for fun
with modern AI tools. We need your help.

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:43.061
Try it now in your browser:
sohitqwer-del.github.io/beta-cutting-room
